  "query_preview": "/SUNDAY THROUGH SATURDAY/...\nIssued at 1226 PM CDT Sat Jul 25 2026\n\nThe heat will stick around through the next few days and a Heat\nAdvisory will be in effect until Tuesday evening. There may \nalso be a few counties over SE KS/SW MO that will need an \nExtreme Heat Warning as the ridge parks over us and cranks up \nthe heat a bit higher in those counties. Either way, it'll be \nhot. Expect highs in the 90s and lower 100s and for temperatures\nto gradually get warmer through the weekend and into the start \nof next week. Heat index values will range from 100 to 110 \ndegrees with little overnight relief with lows in the mid 70s.\n\nThe ridge starts to break down Wednesday into Thursday with\nlow-end (15%) POPs moving in by mid-week with shortwaves\nattempting to move in to the area. Then, a mid-level trough\nmoves through the area on Friday bringing our best chance for\nrain at 20-30% and drop our highs a bit into the upper 80s.",
